WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.735
-Our next guest is the Academy
Award-nominated director

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.236
and producer behind movies

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:05.871
like "The Butler"
and "Precious,"

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:07.474
as well as shows like "Empire."

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.375
His new show,
"Our Kind of People,"

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:12.078
premieres September 21st on Fox.
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:15.248
-Do you know
why I bought this table?

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.984
Because it was the biggest one
I could find!

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:22.188
And I put it in this room
because of the incline...

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.925
so that everyone
sitting around this table

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:30.396
has to raise their head
to look up at me,

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:33.733
a Black man in America

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.937
holding the American dream
in my Black hands.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:41.007
-Please welcome back to
the show Lee Daniels, everyone!

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.409
[ Applause ]

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:46.746
-Yes! [ Laughs ]

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.115
Thank you for being here.
-Hey, buddy.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:52.451
♪♪

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:55.021
-Now, I am always --
Please take a seat.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.289
I am always so happy to see you,

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.057
but I am especially
happy to see --

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.525
-Yeah.
-I want to confirm,

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.927
you are wearing the grill
you wore to the Met Gala.

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:03.863
-I -- Well -- Yeah.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.497
[ Laughs ] All right. I got --

00:01:05.497 --> 00:01:06.900
-Based on the way
you're talking,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.067
this strikes me as your first --
-I got to take --

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.802
I got to take the --
the top ones out.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.037
-You gotta take the top --
-Or the bottom ones out.

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:13.840
-Wait. That's --
Here, you took the bottom --

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.541
-I -- Bec-- Let me
tell you what happened.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:20.313
So, my kids --
I had my tooth removed.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.748
-Okay.
An upper -- a top tooth.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.883
-Yeah, the top tooth
was removed.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.953
And the tooth is not gonna be
available to me until December.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:29.022
-Okay.
-I don't know why.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.456
-It takes that long
to make a tooth?

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.292
-Yeah. It's expensive, too.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.427
-So, my kids said, "Dad,
why don't you get a grill?"

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:36.896
I said, "What the hell's that?"

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.031
They said, "A grill like, you
know, the rappers. The grill."

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:41.367
So I started looking
at these rappers,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.535
these rappers and these grills.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.138
And I got this guy,
Runal the Jeweler.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.540
Runal the Jeweler.
I gave him a shout-out.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.477
-Okay. Great.
-And he put the --

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:54.813
He did this, like, pearls and
diamonds and emeralds and --

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.315
-It was probably more expensive

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.850
than that expensive tooth
you're waiting on.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.152
-Oh, it is.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:03.155
-And so -- Just to cover
the tooth that's missing.

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.725
So I'm at the Met ball.
I'm walking up the stairs.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.393
And I can't talk.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.995
You can hear me trying
to talk with one.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.329
-Yeah.

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:13.165
-And so I took it out,
but I took the wrong one out.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.601
Seth, I took the wrong one out.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:18.070
And the wrong one was the top
one, where my tooth was missing.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.474
So I'm walking around talking,
and my kids are like,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.944
"No! No! Your missing tooth!"
So whatever.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:28.080
-So you ended up with lower
grill, missing-tooth top.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.448
-Missing-tooth top.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.084
-Ultimately
the worst possible outcome.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.719
-But the theme
was, like, Americana.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.420
-Yeah.
-So we got a lot of Americanas

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.155
without any tooth.
You know what I mean?

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.390
So, hey, you know what I mean?

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.025
-That -- I was very happy
about that clip.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:41.694
I feel like you have written --
and tell me --

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.830
I think you write a lot
of great boardroom scenes.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.831
-Thank you.
-I feel like you --

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.267
Your show -- There's something
very powerful about a boardroom

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.936
and people in a boardroom.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.770
And this is a very fun show.
-It is.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.339
-Based on a book, yes?
-It is.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.808
It's based on
"Our Kind of People."

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.576
You know, the good thing
about "Empire"

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.679
was that it enabled me --

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:03.749
So many Black IPs, good ones...
-Yeah.

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.552
-...came to me, and --
and this was one of many.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:11.791
So, it's a great book
about Martha's Vineyard.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.992
-Yeah?

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.595
-And they don't mess
with people of --

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.496
of a certain status
at Martha's Vineyard.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.231
-Yeah.
-White people and Black people.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.933
-It's true.
-The Black people do not mess --

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:25.003
That's old, like --
That's old, uh -- old money.

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:28.040
Old Black money from --
from -- from land, and so --

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.576
-Well, it's a very --
it's been a sort of Black --

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:31.710
For Black wealthy people,

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.913
it's been a vacation
destination forever.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.682
-Yes.
And they don't look --

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.951
They don't look at new --
They're like the Kennedys.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.619
They don't look
at new money as --

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:43.589
as basketball money,
rapper money,

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:45.391
my kind of money,
entertainment money.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.293
They don't look at --
They look down on us.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.694
-Yeah.
-So it's a...

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:51.163
-I have comedy money.
Cannot get a table...

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:52.865
-You can't.
-...at Martha's Vineyard.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.867
-But I heard you crashed
Obama's party.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.036
-I couldn't get an invite
to Obama's party.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.971
-You didn't.
-And I threw it out there.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.340
[ Laughter ]
There was -- I mean --

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.176
-I didn't get one, either.
And I'm telling you something.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.878
It's about that old bluff scene.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.446
-No, you -- Come on.
There were a lot of --

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:12.852
There was a lot of new famous
people at Obama's party.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.721
You could have --
-I did not go.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.388
-Did you get an invite?
-I would not know.

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:17.957
No.
-You didn't get an invite?

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.725
Did you -- Were you holding out
for one at any point?

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:20.859
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.595
[ Laughter ]
-Well, at least,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.363
I think it's very -- I think
it's very nice of both of us

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.599
to be able to admit that --
-Yeah.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.300
-Yeah. Would you --
If they had --

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.802
I thought the perfect outcome

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.904
was to get invited
and then after they pulled

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.305
back the guest list --
-Don't come?

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:34.874
-No, I wanted to be...
-Because of the COVID?

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.175
-...first wave
and then get uninvited

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.710
so I didn't actually
have to go to the party

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.111
but I could say
that I got invited.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.245
-Right.
-Not bad.

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:41.981
-I don't know that I would
have gone anyway.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.416
I'm so paranoid.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.185
I mean, I -- The whole thing
with COVID had me so paranoid.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.220
And even going
to the Met ball was so --

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.456
Like, it is already --
You've been. You know.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.291
It's, like, so --
And then, on top of that,

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.594
can you imagine what it was
like to be in that space...

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.928
-Yeah.
-...thinking,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.865
"Do this person got COVID?
We ain't got no masks on."

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.466
-Yeah.
-You ain't got COVID, do you?

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.368
-Well, the grill
is a natural mask, isn't it?

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.635
-You don't have COVID?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:04.970
-I don't have -- So, wait.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.640
You mentioned IP, which
is intellectual property, right?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.308
-Yeah. Mm-hmm.
-And another one

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:10.976
you're producing is
"The Wonder Years."

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.079
So, this is -- You know,
this is a very iconic show

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.480
that's being remade.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.881
I didn't want
to do that, either.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.749
-You didn't want to do that?
-I didn't want to.

00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:19.919
-'Cause you were worried
about the -- the history of it?

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.420
-Well, it's a classic.
-Yeah, it is.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.856
-I mean, it is, like, a classic.
How can you -- They came to me.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.625
And I was -- So I didn't
want to direct it.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.828
I didn't want to write it. I
just didn't want to mess it up.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:32.631
So, I found a great
showrunner/writer, Saladin,

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:35.768
who -- who had
a good take on it

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.103
and who really understood
the nuance

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:41.140
of the African-American
experience at that time.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:45.277
I wanted to show my family
and so many other Black families

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:49.348
that were middle-class
and could --

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.550
But we aren't represented
that way in the '60s,

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.352
in the '70s,
in the early '80s.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.586
We are specific.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:58.291
And so this is a middle-class
Black family...

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.993
and what --
what that world is like.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.028
And it's exactly the same tone.
Fred Savage directed it.

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:04.831
-Oh, that's wonderful.
-It's exactly the same --

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:07.733
exactly the same tone
as -- as "Wonder Years."

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.835
And it's good.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:11.203
-That's great.
-It's really good.

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:12.605
-Speaking of really good...
-What?

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.006
-...another show
you're producing.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.641
-What?
-Comedian Ms. Pat.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:19.145
So, we met Ms. Pat.
I met her on Zoom.

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.379
She has stayed with me.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:23.482
The Ms. Pat experience
left a mark on me.

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:24.917
I was very taken with Ms. Pat.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.718
She's a very funny person
that I was not aware of.

00:06:26.718 --> 00:06:28.387
How much did you know
about her before you --

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:29.422
-Nothing.
-Nothing, okay.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.857
-Nothing!
As much as you did.

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.591
-Somebody said, "We want you
to meet this woman, Ms. Pat"?

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:33.659
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.794
-Brian Grazer
wanted me to meet her.

00:06:35.794 --> 00:06:37.463
My partner,
my producing partner.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:40.399
And he was in the middle
of "Empire."

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:44.837
And I'd never seen anything --
witnessed anything like her.

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.772
The closest thing I could
think of was Roseanne.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:47.740
-Yeah.
-On steroids.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.941
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.710
-Literally on crack,
which she was selling.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.045
Pat was selling.
-Yeah.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:56.382
-And we were trying
to get the show sold,

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:59.519
and people weren't
buying it, you know?

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.053
And --

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:02.921
[ Laughs ]

00:07:02.921 --> 00:07:05.124
I mean, you know,
she's a crack dealer

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:08.227
that turned her life around
and now is a stand-up comic.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.129
-Yeah.
-You can't -- You can't --

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.330
Seth, you can't make it up.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.098
-Well, I --
it's funny to think about.

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:14.766
You know,
'cause it's very sterile,

00:07:14.766 --> 00:07:16.736
those environments where
you go and pitch TV shows.

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:18.037
-Yeah.
-And for someone --

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.972
It's very funny to think of,
like, you guys walking in

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.607
and, like, her pitching
that show to executives.

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:26.144
How did it go when -- when she
sort of told her story to them?

00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:28.514
-I told her, I said,
"No surprises, Pat."

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.682
-Yeah.
-"No surprises.

00:07:30.682 --> 00:07:32.184
Please, no surprises."

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.587
And she, of course,
gave me the surprise

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:36.288
in front of all these
white people.

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:38.323
She says, "You know,
my nipple got shot off.

00:07:38.323 --> 00:07:41.193
[ Laughter ]
But I put it back on."

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:43.562
And then she says "You know,
my mama shot my brains --

00:07:43.562 --> 00:07:45.765
shot my -- shot my --
shot a bullet through my brain."

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:47.599
And I'm --
And these cats are like --

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:49.001
These suits -- I mean, you know.
-Yeah.

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:51.837
-I mean, these suits
are like, "What the...?"

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:53.505
-Exactly!
-But we sold it.

00:07:53.505 --> 00:07:54.706
And it's incredible.

00:07:54.706 --> 00:07:57.476
I think it's --
it's an important show.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:58.844
-It's really wonderful.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.946
-And I should note, like,
it's -- it's a family show.

00:08:00.946 --> 00:08:02.347
-Very Norman Lear.
Very Norman Lear.

00:08:02.347 --> 00:08:03.682
-Yeah. That's -- I mean, I think
we're -- you know, we're --

00:08:03.682 --> 00:08:05.083
we're talking about sort of
the most extreme parts

00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:06.919
of her story,
but it's really authentic.

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.820
And the part about it
that's really cool,

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.222
is it's -- oh, this is, like --

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:12.225
Her family is like a lot
of other families, as well.

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:13.692
Maybe a different backstory.

00:08:13.692 --> 00:08:15.360
But the way families interact.
It's a really great show.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.529
-Yeah, it really is.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:18.931
Jordan Cooper
is our showrunner.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:22.401
A young kid, 26 years old.

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.871
Has never written anything.
And I'm real excited about it.

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.572
-Well, congratulations
on everything.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.507
It's always such a delight
to have you here.

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:30.108
-Thank you.
-Really appreciate it.

00:08:30.108 --> 00:08:32.879
"Our Kind of People" premieres
September 21st on Fox.

